title: Claim identity and liveness
desc:20
A pid is meaningful only relative to a process table and only until it is
recycled, so a claim records pid.starttime@runtime, where runtime is boot id
plus uid plus pid namespace, derived rather than stored. Each part closed a
real hole: a stored checkout id survived reboots, kill -0 reported another
user's live process as dead, and containers sharing a checkout shared an id
but not a process table.

Agents with no reachable process table carry a lease instead: an expiry on
line 1, no heartbeat. PIDLY_AGENT requires PIDLY_LEASE, since an agent that
can neither be checked nor expire would wedge a ticket forever.

Underlying rule: never report dead without positive evidence. Unknown
resolves to unverifiable, because calling a live claim dead puts two agents
on one ticket.

Done: implemented in bin/pidly, covered by tests/identity.sh (18 cases).
